              %p and hence the result.
          %p
            The last two examples can also be considered as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+isomorphisms"} exceptional isomorphisms
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+Lie+groups"} classical Lie groups
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#group_extension Group extension
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              We have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Spin
                      %mi c
                    %mo →
                    %mi SO
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U(1) \to Spin^c \to SO
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Spin
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1) \to Spin^c
              is the canonical inclusion into the defining product
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo ×
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi Spin
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mn 2
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1) \to Spin \times U(1) \to Spin \times_{\mathbb{Z}_2} U(1)
          %h3#general General
          %h3#AsHomotopyFiberOfSmoothW3
            As the homotopy fiber of the smooth
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi W
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{W}_3
          %p We discuss in the following that
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the universal third
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+Stiefel-Whitney+class"} integral Stiefel-Whitney class
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_3
                has an essentially unique lift from
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≃
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                to
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            %li
              %p
                the smooth
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %msup
                        %mi Spin
                        %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Smooth
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}Spin^c \in Smooth\infty Grpd
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi W
                          %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{W}_3
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle"} circle 2-bundle
                over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi SO
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B} SO
                classified by
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi W
                          %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{W}_3
          #SpinCAsHomotopyPullbackOfW2AndC1.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              We have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %msup
                              %mi Spin
                              %mi c
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi B
                                %mi det
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                      %mi c
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mi mod
                                  %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi SO
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                    %mi w
                                  %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 2
                            %msub
                              %mi ℤ
                              %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbf{B} Spin^c
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\mathbf{B}det}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}U(1)
                    \\\
                    \\big\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\big\downarrow{}^{\mathrlap{\mathbf{c}_1 mod 2}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathbf{B} SO
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\mathbf{w}_2}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}^2 \mathbb{Z}_2
                    }
            %p
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the right morphism is the universal first
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+class"} Chern class
                  modulo 2;
              %li
                %p
                  the bottom morphism is the universal second
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stiefel-Whitney+class"} Stiefel-Whitney class
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We present the sitation as usual in the projective
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
              over
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-anafunctors"} ∞-anafunctors
            %p
              The first
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+class"} Chern class
              is given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-anafunctor"} ∞-anafunctor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo →
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                    %mi c
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo →
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo =
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 2
                            %mi ℤ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ≃
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbf{B}(\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{R})
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\mathbf{c}_1}{\to}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}(\mathbb{Z} \to 1)
                    \=
                    \\mathbf{B}^2 \mathbb{Z}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathbf{B} U(1)
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G_1 \to G_0)
              denotes a presentation of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-group"} strict 2-group
              by a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
            %p
              The second
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stiefel-Whitney+class"} Stiefel-Whitney class
              is given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi ℤ
                              %mn 2
                            %mo →
                            %mi Spin
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                    %mi w
                                  %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi ℤ
                              %mn 2
                            %mo →
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo =
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 2
                            %msub
                              %mi ℤ
                              %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ≃
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi SO
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbf{B}(\mathbb{Z}_2 \to Spin)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\mathbf{w}_2}{\to}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}(\mathbb{Z}_2 \to 1)
                    \=
                    \\mathbf{B}^2 \mathbb{Z}_2
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathbf{B} SO
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Notice that the top horizontal morphism here is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
            %p
              Therefore the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              in question is (as discussed there) given by the ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Q
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo →
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi ℤ
                              %mn 2
                            %mo →
                            %mi Spin
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 2
                            %msub
                              %mi ℤ
                              %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Q
                    \&amp;\to&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}(\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{R})
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbf{B}(\mathbb{Z}_2 \to Spin)
                    \&amp;\to&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}^2 \mathbb{Z}_2
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              This pullback is
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ∂
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}(\mathbb{Z} \stackrel{\partial}{\to} Spin \times \mathbb{R})
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi n
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi mod
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\partial\colon n \mapsto ( n \,mod\, 2 , n)
                    \\,.
            %p This is equivalent to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ∂
                            %mi Spin
                            %mo ×
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi ℤ
                              %mn 2
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∂
                                %mo ′
                            %mi Spin
                            %mo ×
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mn 2
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi ℤ
                              %mn 2
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∂
                                %mo ′
                            %mi Spin
                            %mo ×
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    (\mathbb{Z} \stackrel{\partial}{\to} Spin \times \mathbb{R})
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    (\mathbb{Z}_2 \stackrel{\partial'}{\to} Spin \times (\mathbb{R}/2\mathbb{Z}))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    (\mathbb{Z}_2 \stackrel{\partial'}{\to} Spin \times U(1))
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,,
            %p
              (notice the non-standard identification
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1) \simeq \mathbb{R}/(2\mathbb{Z})
              here, which is important below in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalDeterminantLineBundleMap"}
              for the identification of
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi det
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} det
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial'
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal"} diagonal
              embedding of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi σ
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\partial'\colon \sigma \mapsto (\sigma, \sigma)
                    \\,.
            %p This in turn is equivalent to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spin
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 2
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{B} (Spin \times_{\mathbb{Z}_2} U(1))
                    \\,,
            %p
              which is def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DirectDefinitionOfSpinC"}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Compare this with the similar but different
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              that defines the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi Spin
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi SO
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                    %mi w
                                  %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 2
                            %msub
                              %mi ℤ
                              %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbf{B}Spin &amp;\to&amp; *
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbf{B}SO &amp;\stackrel{\mathbf{w}_2}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B}^2 \mathbb{Z}_2
                    }
          #UniversalDeterminantLineBundleMap.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Under the identificaton
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Spin
                      %mi c
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Spin
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 2
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin^c \simeq Spin \underset{\mathbb{Z}_2}{\times} U(1)
              the “universal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/determinant+line+bundle"} determinant line bundle
              map”
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi det
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi Spin
                      %mi c
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    det \colon Spin^c \to U(1)
            %p is given in components by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mn 2
                    %mi c
